      </table>
      <div>&#160;</div>
      <div style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 36pt; color: #000000;">Sales and marketing expenses increased by $3.9 million, or 63%, to $10.1 million for the year ended December 31, 2022 as compared to $6.2 million for the year ended December 31,
        2021. The increase was primarily due to:</div>
      <div>&#160;</div>
      <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" id="zed1a0ceb502448bdaf23188e2051e4f2" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: #000000;">

          <tr>
            <td style="width: 36pt;"><br>
            </td>
            <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; color: #000000;">&#8226;</td>
            <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top; text-align: justify;">
              <div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">An increase of $2.8 million in stock-based compensation due to the issuance of stock option and restricted stock unit awards;</div>
            </td>
          </tr>

      </table>
      <div>&#160;</div>
      <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" id="z5f2e76d5fed843c5a8afafc23b7ec2c1" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: #000000;">

          <tr>
            <td style="width: 36pt;"><br>
            </td>
            <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; color: #000000;">&#8226;</td>
            <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top; text-align: justify;">
              <div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">An&#160; increase of $0.9 million in personnel-related costs resulting from an increase in headcount and higher salaries;</div>
            </td>
          </tr>

      </table>
      <div> <br>
      </div>
